of Leibniz’s argument should strike you as a plausible one.","targetRectangle":{"y":-266.55548095703125,"x":722.87930297851562,"width":285.68115234375,"height":192}},{"text":"Leibniz’s argument","targetRectangle":{"y":111.07279968261719,"x":23.10901113729614,"width":69.55224839838084,"height":42}},{"text":"objections to the ","targetRectangle":{"y":209.60308837890625,"x":43.822395491363324,"width":40.52197265625,"height":22}},{"text":"PSR","targetRectangle":{"y":231.60308837890625,"x":54.30994455545455,"width":16.55419921875,"height":11}},{"text":"the","targetRectangle":{"y":25.480010986328125,"x":49.871708560159078,"width":13.212890625,"height":13}},{"text":"PSR","targetRectangle":{"y":38.480010986328125,"x":47.281376806803429,"width":18.393554687499993,"height":13}},{"text":"We found reason to doubt the idea that, if there is a first cause, then God exists. Do similar doubts apply to premise (8) of Leibniz’s argument?","targetRectangle":{"y":-487.66790771484375,"x":391.72537231445312,"width":298.14453125,"height":192}},{"text":"Here we can say things similar to the things we said about quasi-theism when we were discussing the first cause hypothesis. ","targetRectangle":{"y":-242.30906677246094,"x":187.13197326660156,"width":757.94677734375,"height":64}},{"text":"1. The fact that there are contingent things is contingent.","targetRectangle":{"y":811.64959716796875,"x":134.06908416748047,"width":463.71875,"height":60.799999237060547}},{"text":"2. Every contingent fact has an explanation. (PSR)","targetRectangle":{"y":869.24959564208984,"x":134.06908416748047,"width":436.71875,"height":60.799999237060547}},{"text":"3. The fact that there are contingent things has an explanation. (1,2)","targetRectangle":{"y":926.84959411621094,"x":134.06908416748047,"width":368.4814453125,"height":89.599998474121094}},{"text":"4. The fact that there are contingent things can’t be explained by any contingent thing.","targetRectangle":{"y":1013.2495918273926,"x":134.06908416748047,"width":491.013671875,"height":89.599998474121094}},{"text":"5. The fact that there are contingent things is explained by some thing which is not contingent. (3,4)","targetRectangle":{"y":1099.6495895385742,"x":134.06908416748047,"width":491.013671875,"height":118.39999771118164}},{"text":"6. The fact that there are contingent things is explained by some necessary thing. (5)","targetRectangle":{"y":1214.8495864868164,"x":134.06908416748047,"width":491.013671875,"height":89.599998474121094}},{"text":"7. There is a necessary thing which explains the existence of contingent things. (6)","targetRectangle":{"y":1301.249584197998,"x":134.06908416748047,"width":491.30859375,"height":89.599998474121094}},{"text":"8. If there is a necessary thing which explains the existence of contingent things, then God exists.","targetRectangle":{"y":1387.6495819091797,"x":134.06908416748047,"width":463.71875,"height":118.39999771118164}},{"text":"————————————————","targetRectangle":{"y":1502.8495788574219,"x":134.06908416748047,"width":218.359375,"height":32}},{"text":"C. God exists. (7,8) (7,8)","targetRectangle":{"y":1531.6495780944824,"x":134.06908416748047,"width":354.833984375,"height":32}},{"text":"The  cosmological argument","targetRectangle":{"y":-747.1947021484375,"x":230.01147031784058,"width":330.72998477218789,"height":32}},{"text":"We can again consider the hypotheses of simple theism and simple atheism, and now consider alongside them the quasi-theistic hypothesis that the universe was created by a being with the unusual property that it is literally impossible for that being not to exist.","targetRectangle":{"y":-145.87458801269531,"x":186.22865295410156,"width":759.75341796875,"height":128}},{"text":"1. The fact that there are contingent things is contingent.","targetRectangle":{"y":-669.849365234375,"x":141.89885711669922,"width":498.6572265625,"height":55.800000369548798}},{"text":"2. Every contingent fact has an explanation. (PSR)","targetRectangle":{"y":-620.2493644952774,"x":141.89885711669922,"width":419.921875,"height":55.800000369548798}},{"text":"3. The fact that there are contingent things has an explanation. (1,2)","targetRectangle":{"y":-570.64936375617981,"x":141.89885711669922,"width":498.6572265625,"height":55.800000369548798}},{"text":"4. The fact that there are contingent things can’t be explained by any contingent thing.","targetRectangle":{"y":-521.04936301708221,"x":141.89885711669922,"width":498.6572265625,"height":80.600000739097595}},{"text":"5. The fact that there are contingent things is explained by some thing which is not contingent. (3,4)","targetRectangle":{"y":-446.64936190843582,"x":141.89885711669922,"width":498.6572265625,"height":80.600000739097595}},{"text":"6. The fact that there are contingent things is explained by some necessary thing. (5)","targetRectangle":{"y":-372.24936079978943,"x":141.89885711669922,"width":498.6572265625,"height":80.600000739097595}},{"text":"7. There is a necessary thing which explains the existence of contingent things. (6)","targetRectangle":{"y":-297.84935969114304,"x":141.89885711669922,"width":472.412109375,"height":80.600000739097595}},{"text":"8. If there is a necessary thing which explains the existence of contingent things, then God exists.","targetRectangle":{"y":-223.44935858249664,"x":141.89885711669922,"width":511.77978515625,"height":80.600000739097595}},{"text":"----------------------------------","targetRectangle":{"y":-149.04935747385025,"x":141.89885711669922,"width":446.1669921875,"height":31}},{"text":"C. God exists. (7,8)","targetRectangle":{"y":-124.24935710430145,"x":141.89885711669922,"width":262.451171875,"height":31}},{"text":"We can again consider the hypotheses of simple theism and simple atheism, and now consider alongside them the quasi-theistic hypothesis that the universe was created by a being with the unusual property that it is literally impossible for that being not to exist.","targetRectangle":{"y":-647.89453125,"x":707.72427368164062,"w